# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every working copy.
#
# Git for Windows sets core.autocrlf=true system-wide, so without this every
# checkout turned the (LF) repository into CRLF files on disk: `gofmt -l`
# flagged the whole tree, CI's gofmt check could only be reproduced by
# stripping \r first, and files written by LF-producing tools sat next to
# CRLF ones. eol=lf applies whatever core.autocrlf says, on every clone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF on disk: cmd.exe mis-parses labels and
# multi-line blocks in LF batch files.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.vbs text eol=crlf

# Binary artefacts: never touched.
*.xlsx binary
*.db binary
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary

# TDTP packets are byte-exact artefacts. docs/REGISTRATION_DOSSIER.md cites their
# bytes as the BOF/EOF signatures submitted to PRONOM, so git must never
# translate line endings on them — a CRLF checkout would hand a reviewer a file
# the implementation does not produce.
*.tdtp -text
